* START-HISTORY:
* 10 Nov 26 Windows port - from Linux 0cbb8b93 (12 Oct), abcda0c1 (S.63), d7cda813 (S.64), d049d8bb (S.96 M6; the S.67 journal
*               call is not carried, the master copies having been retired): RELEASE_1.1 146.  OS.EXECUTE runs PowerShell here, so
*               the copy is Copy-Item and the append a .NET byte append (binary safe); the gates are asked as on Linux, as the account,
*               for both paths and before the existence test.  Messages are Linux's + 1005.
* 13 Oct 26 dm  S.63: asks the OS-access gate (K$PATH.OK) for both paths; status -4 is a path outside the account
*               for an account without OS.EXECUTE.  A measured !OSCOPY by such an account read AND wrote files
*               outside its directory.
* 12 Oct 26 dm  1.2-0 openQM refs 517 (append) and 369 (iOSCOPY, the directory form).  The syntax is SD's own.
* END-HISTORY
*
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   CALL !OSCOPY(source, target, mode, status)
*   CALL !IOSCOPY(source, target, status)
*
* !OSCOPY copies one operating system file.  Mode 0 refuses if the target
* exists, 1 replaces it, 2 appends the source to the end of it (the target
* is made if it is not there).  !IOSCOPY copies a file or a whole directory
* tree, replacing what is in the way; a directory is copied INTO the target
* if the target is an existing directory.
*
* Status is 0 when it worked.  -1 is a path that is null or holds a single
* quote, -2 a source that is not there, -3 a target that exists (mode 0),
* -4 a path outside the account's own directory for an account that has not
* been given OS.EXECUTE (modify.account name os-on), and anything else the
* status of the copy command.  Both run with the permissions of the user,
* like OS.EXECUTE, and are asked the same question.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
$no.xref
subroutine oscopy(source, target, mode, status)
$catalog !OSCOPY

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h

   status = 0
   gosub check.paths
   if status # 0 then return

   if mode = 0 and ospath(target, OS$EXISTS) then
      status = -3
      return
   end

* 10 Nov 26 Windows port: PowerShell in place of cp and cat.  Both paths are inside single quotes, where PowerShell
*   expands nothing ($ and the backquote are literal), and a single quote was refused above.  -LiteralPath and the .NET
*   calls take the name as it is (no wildcards).  A failure is a terminating error that the catch turns into exit 1, so
*   os.error() is not 0.
*   PowerShell is given the path as Windows spells it (kernel(K$WINPATH), absolute), which is the file the gates above
*   were asked about: SD reads /x/y from the runtime's root and PowerShell would read it from the drive's, so the name
*   as typed could be vetted as one file and copied as another.  A path the runtime cannot convert is refused (-1).
   wsource = kernel(K$WINPATH, source)
   wtarget = kernel(K$WINPATH, target)
   if wsource = '' or wtarget = '' or index(wsource, "'", 1) or index(wtarget, "'", 1) then
      status = -1
      return
   end

   begin case
      case mode = 2
         cmd = "try { $b = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes('" : wsource : "'); "
         cmd := "$s = [System.IO.File]::Open('" : wtarget : "', [System.IO.FileMode]::Append, [System.IO.FileAccess]::Write); "
         cmd := "try { $s.Write($b, 0, $b.Length) } finally { $s.Close() } } catch { exit 1 }"
      case 1
         cmd = "try { Copy-Item -LiteralPath '" : wsource : "' -Destination '" : wtarget : "' -Force -ErrorAction Stop } catch { exit 1 }"
   end case

   out = ''
   os.execute cmd capturing out
   status = os.error()
   return

check.paths:
   if source = '' or target = '' or index(source, "'", 1) or index(target, "'", 1) then
      status = -1
   end else
* 13 Oct 26 dm - S.63.  This program is $internal, so the kernel does not ask the account's gate on its behalf and
*   the copy runs with the permissions of the operating-system user.  It is asked here, as the account, for BOTH paths
*   and BEFORE the existence test, so that -2 does not tell an account without OS access which files exist elsewhere.
      if not(kernel(K$PATH.OK, source)) or not(kernel(K$PATH.OK, target)) then
         status = -4
      end else if not(kernel(K$EDIT.OS.OK, target)) then
*        17 Oct 26 dm - S.64: a copy INTO a program file, a dictionary or a VOC (any component of the target below the account) is a
*        change to it and needs the gate.  Asked for the target only: reading them is not a change.
         status = -4
      end else
         if not(ospath(source, OS$EXISTS)) then
            status = -2
         end
      end
   end
   return
end

* END-CODE
